---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="The Whetstone — structural logic auditor for written arguments"
  description="Audit the reasoning in any argument. 26 fallacy patterns, Toulmin decomposition, counterargument generation, citation audit, and evidence-weighted likelihood. Free for readers. Pro tools for writers."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-24 pb-20">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl sm:text-6xl text-gray-900 leading-[1.1] mb-6">
        See the structure<br class="hidden sm:block" /> behind every argument.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-10">
        The Whetstone analyses the reasoning in any text — what's claimed, what evidence is offered,
        where the logic breaks down, and the strongest opposing case the writer didn't engage with.
        Not a verdict on who's right. A structural view of how the argument works.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a
          href="/reader"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-indigo-600 text-white text-sm font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-indigo-700 transition-colors"
        >
          Try the audit — free
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
        </a>
        <a
          href="/creator/studio"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors"
        >
          Open Creator Studio
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What it finds — feature grid -->
    <section class="border-t border-gray-200 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-10">What the engine analyses</h2>

        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-0 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <div class="p-6 border-b lg:border-b-0 sm:border-r border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">🔬</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Argument structure</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              Toulmin decomposition — claim, grounds, warrant, weakest link. The skeleton of the argument, stripped of rhetoric.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 border-b lg:border-b-0 lg:border-r border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">⚠️</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">26 reasoning patterns</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              From Post Hoc to Motte-and-Bailey, Selection Bias to Genetic Fallacy. Verbatim quotes, severity, confidence.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 border-b border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">⚔️</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Counterarguments</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              The 2–3 strongest objections a thoughtful opponent would deploy — each with its own Toulmin structure.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 sm:border-r border-b lg:border-b-0 border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">📎</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Citation audit</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              Every cited URL fetched and checked — does the source actually support the claim it's cited for?
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 lg:border-r border-b lg:border-b-0 border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">🧭</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Philosophical commitments</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              The ethical, epistemic, and political framework the argument operates within — made visible.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">📊</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Evidence-weighted likelihood</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              For empirical claims, we search 200M+ academic papers and assess scientific consensus. Value claims are flagged as such.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Two products -->
    <section class="border-t border-gray-200">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">

          <a href="/reader" class="group block rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-8 hover:border-indigo-300 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-500 mb-3">Reader</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl text-gray-900 group-hover:text-indigo-700 transition-colors mb-3">
              Audit any argument
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Paste text or a URL. The engine maps the structure, flags reasoning issues, and shows you the argument's bones. Free — no account required.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-600 group-hover:text-indigo-800">
              Open the Reader →
            </p>
          </a>

          <a href="/creator" class="group block rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-8 hover:border-amber-300 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-600 mb-3">Creator</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl text-gray-900 group-hover:text-amber-700 transition-colors mb-3">
              Stress-test your writing
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Full audit suite, counterarguments, citation checking, revision tracking, and inline highlights. For students, journalists, and professional writers.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-600 group-hover:text-amber-800">
              Open Creator Studio →
            </p>
          </a>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Trust strip -->
    <section class="border-t border-gray-200 bg-gray-50">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-8 text-center">
          <div>
            <p class="text-2xl font-serif text-gray-900 mb-1">26</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Reasoning patterns detected</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-2xl font-serif text-gray-900 mb-1">11</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Analytical lenses</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-2xl font-serif text-gray-900 mb-1">200M+</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Papers searchable via Semantic Scholar</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Open source + privacy -->
    <section class="border-t border-gray-200">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Open source</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Every prompt and schema is auditable in the public repository. A tool that shapes
            how people read arguments should be transparent about how it works.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Daniell-44/The_Whetstone_Project" class="text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 transition-colors" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            View on GitHub →
          </a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Privacy-first</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            No analytics. No tracking cookies. No advertising. We do not sell, share, or profile your data.
            Audit text is processed and discarded — never stored.
          </p>
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 transition-colors">
            Privacy policy →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Base>
